course: dictionary
lesson: 2396
title: One word, many meanings: curse
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word curse can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. In fairy tales, «the witch's curse» is a magic spell that brings bad luck.
explain: In everyday talk, a curse can be a rude word said when someone is angry. To curse, as a verb, means to swear or use bad words. When a character curses, the reader learns they are very angry, or that bad magic is at work.
explain: A curse can also mean something that keeps causing trouble. The clue is in the sentence, not in the word itself. Ask yourself: is there magic here, is someone angry, or is something causing ongoing trouble? Then pick the meaning that fits.
fact: A curse is a magic spell or wish that something bad will happen to someone.
fact: A curse can be a rude word said when someone is angry, and to curse means to swear.
fact: «The witch cursed the prince» means she put a magic spell on him.
fact: «Gosh darn it» is a polite form of a stronger curse, so people say it instead of the rude word.
fact: Phrases to know: put a curse on, under a curse, curse under your breath, the curse of.
exercise: «So when a grandmother drops a cup and cries "Gosh darn it!", she is saying a much stronger curse in a polite shape that nobody minds.» What is «Gosh darn it» a polite form of? | A magic spell that breaks cups | A map of the town | *A much stronger curse | A kind song for a birthday
exercise: «The witch cursed the princess and she fell into a long sleep.» What does cursed mean here? | Sang her to sleep | Gave her a birthday present | *Put a magic spell on her
exercise: «The old car was a curse on the family, always breaking down.» What does curse mean here? | A song | A fast race | *Something that keeps causing trouble | A kind present
test: To curse someone means what? | *To put a magic spell on them | To count their steps | To give them a hug
test: A curse can be a rude word said when someone is angry. What is it called? | A type of tree | A greeting | *A swear word
exam: In which sentence does curse mean a magic spell? | *The witch's curse turned the prince into a frog | The cat slept on the mat | We went to the park after school | The river runs past the old mill
